<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michoacán</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michoacán is a state of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, stretching from the Pacific coast to the volcanic highlands, with its capital at Morelia. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purepecha-empire">Purépecha</a> state, which resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztecs</a> and submitted to the Spanish between 1522 and 1530. In the colonial period it became a bishopric under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-de-quiroga">Vasco de Quiroga</a>, and it was a key region in the war of independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/michoacan.jpg" alt="Michoacán" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mauricio C. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cerro_Patamban.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
